We'll be shooting a test of courage!

398
00:12:00,990 --> 00:12:02,540
STAFF A: Let's all give it our best!

399
00:12:02,860 --> 00:12:06,130
STAFF B: Can someone who's free go check 
on the speakers in storage?

400
00:12:06,130 --> 00:12:08,260
UTAGE: Yes! I can go check!

401
00:12:08,260 --> 00:12:10,970
STAFF A: Could you split up into 
groups of two and three?

402
00:12:10,970 --> 00:12:12,310
ARIMOTO: Is everything ready?

403
00:12:12,310 --> 00:12:13,430
STAFF D: Yes, sir!

404
00:12:22,120 --> 00:12:23,810
UTAGE: I can't seem to find them...

405
00:12:23,810 --> 00:12:26,110
UTAGE: Did I check the wrong place?

406
00:12:27,010 --> 00:12:27,990
UTAGE: Huh?

407
00:12:31,130 --> 00:12:32,780
STAFF A: What's going on with the speakers?

408
00:12:32,780 --> 00:12:36,340
STAFF B: I had the part-timer go check on them, 
but she's not back yet.

409
00:12:36,340 --> 00:12:38,660
STAFF A: Don't have a part-timer 
do any final checks!

410
00:12:38,660 --> 00:12:40,720
STAFF A: We're about to start shooting any minute!

411
00:12:40,720 --> 00:12:42,150
STAFF C: I'll go check on her.

412
00:12:42,150 --> 00:12:44,520
STAFF C: The speakers are in the storage shed 
behind the school building, right?

413
00:12:44,520 --> 00:12:47,380
STAFF A: Yeah. There are two storage sheds, 
so go to the right one.

414
00:12:47,380 --> 00:12:49,120
STAFF A: They're not in the one behind the gym!

415
00:12:49,120 --> 00:12:49,870
STAFF C: Got it!

416
00:12:49,870 --> 00:12:52,220
FUJITA: I'm so sorry about our staff.

417
00:12:52,220 --> 00:12:54,730
NATSUKI: What's up? Is there some kind of trouble?

418
00:12:54,730 --> 00:12:56,250
TAMON: I'll go look for her!

419
00:12:56,250 --> 00:12:56,680
NATSUKI: Huh?

420
00:12:56,680 --> 00:12:59,980
FUJITA: Hey, Tamon! You better come right back!

421
00:13:02,430 --> 00:13:04,500
UTAGE: Someone, please!

422
00:13:05,730 --> 00:13:10,290
UTAGE: Why won't it open? At this rate, 
the shoot will be affected...

423
00:13:10,290 --> 00:13:11,660
UTAGE: What should I do?

424
00:13:11,660 --> 00:13:12,940
UTAGE: What should I do?

425
00:13:13,380 --> 00:13:14,810
TAMON: Kinoshita-san?

426
00:13:14,810 --> 00:13:15,950
UTAGE: Gloomyhara-san?!

427
00:13:19,320 --> 00:13:21,430
TAMON: Thank goodness you're safe...

428
00:13:24,020 --> 00:13:25,670
UTAGE: Gloomyhara-san.

429
00:13:26,590 --> 00:13:29,390
TAMON: I didn't know what I was going to do 
if I found you as a corpse.

430
00:13:47,940 --> 00:13:50,650
UTAGE: Someone! Please!

431
00:13:51,280 --> 00:13:54,690
UTAGE: Someone, please! We're in here!

432
00:13:53,380 --> 00:13:54,780
TAMON: What are we going to do?

433
00:13:54,780 --> 00:13:56,230
TAMON: What if this door never opens again

434
00:13:56,230 --> 00:13:58,230
TAMON: and both the shoot and show are ruined

435
00:13:58,230 --> 00:14:00,290
TAMON: and Kinoshita-san 
and I end up as mummies, 

436
00:14:00,290 --> 00:14:03,680
TAMON: and we end up finished both 
socially and physically?!

437
00:14:03,680 --> 00:14:06,660
TAMON: It'd be fine if it were just me, 
but Kinoshita-san can't end up wrinkly!

438
00:14:06,660 --> 00:14:07,470
TAMON: I'm so sorry!

439
00:14:07,470 --> 00:14:10,450
TAMON: They say that I'm rejuvenating eye candy, 
but that doesn't actually exist!

440
00:14:03,140 --> 00:14:04,230
UTAGE: This isn't good.

441
00:14:04,230 --> 00:14:08,470
UTAGE: Even if the shoot resumed, he won't
 go back to Hottiehara-kun after this.

442
00:14:08,570 --> 00:14:11,280
UTAGE: Please calm down. It'll be okay!

443
00:14:11,280 --> 00:14:15,560
UTAGE: If you're missing, someone will notice 
immediately and come open the door.

444
00:14:15,560 --> 00:14:16,850
TAMON: But what if it doesn't open?

445
00:14:16,850 --> 00:14:18,350
UTAGE: It will!

446
00:14:19,310 --> 00:14:21,030
STAFF A: Do you see the part-timer girl?

447
00:14:21,030 --> 00:14:22,020
STAFF B: She's not here.

448
00:14:22,020 --> 00:14:23,720
ARIMOTO: Damn it, where'd they go?

449
00:14:23,720 --> 00:14:26,510
ARIMOTO: Now the shoot's gonna 
have to pause... Oh.

450
00:14:35,240 --> 00:14:37,430
UTAGE: I-It'll be okay! It'll be okay!

451
00:14:37,430 --> 00:14:39,410
UTAGE: I'm sure everything will work out!

452
00:14:43,050 --> 00:14:47,990
UTAGE: If Tamon-kun's shoot gets ruined...

453
00:14:57,330 --> 00:15:00,850
TAMON: You're not okay, are you, Kinoshita-san?

454
00:15:00,850 --> 00:15:04,070
UTAGE: Huh? Th-That's not...

455
00:15:07,270 --> 00:15:08,330
UTAGE: What?!

456
00:15:09,530 --> 00:15:12,010
TAMON: You must be tired, Kinoshita-san.

457
00:15:12,010 --> 00:15:13,190
UTAGE: I'm not, though.

458
00:15:13,530 --> 00:15:15,110
TAMON: You are!

459
00:15:15,480 --> 00:15:20,490
TAMON: There's no way you could make 
those fans instantly either.

460
00:15:21,100 --> 00:15:22,380
TAMON: I figured you made them

461
00:15:22,380 --> 00:15:24,840
TAMON: after finding out 
about the training camp...

462
00:15:29,990 --> 00:15:35,900
UTAGE: N-Now that you mention it, 
I might be a little tired... maybe?

463
00:15:36,940 --> 00:15:42,180
TAMON: I've been watching you more than 
you realize, Kinoshita-san...

464
00:15:45,730 --> 00:15:48,260
STAFF A: Hey! Is someone in here?

465
00:15:48,260 --> 00:15:49,480
STAFF A: If you're in there, say something!

466
00:15:49,480 --> 00:15:50,440
STAFF B: Let's open the door.

467
00:15:50,440 --> 00:15:52,630
UTAGE: We're here! We're in here!

468
00:15:54,990 --> 00:15:58,290
UTAGE: I'm so sorry! I should've 
been more careful.

469
00:15:58,290 --> 00:16:02,030
TAMON: No! The door was broken 
and shut on its own!

470
00:16:03,590 --> 00:16:05,560
KEITO: Hey, Tamon! Are you okay?

471
00:16:05,560 --> 00:16:07,700
KEITO: That woman didn't try 
to do anything to you, did she?

472
00:16:08,860 --> 00:16:11,080
TAMON: What do you even mean by that?

473
00:16:14,790 --> 00:16:17,260
ARIMOTO: Er, everyone... I'm sorry!

474
00:16:18,610 --> 00:16:21,480
ARIMOTO: This is actually all my fault.

475
00:16:21,480 --> 00:16:24,590
ARIMOTO: The storage shed behind the gym 
wouldn't open from the inside, right?

476
00:16:24,590 --> 00:16:28,230
ARIMOTO: I actually rigged it so that 
it'd only open from the outside.

477
00:16:28,230 --> 00:16:31,260
ARIMOTO: I wanted to get some footage 
of Tamon-kun genuinely being surprised.

478
00:16:31,260 --> 00:16:32,190
ARIMOTO: Tee-hee!

479
00:16:32,190 --> 00:16:33,070
UTAGE: Whut?!

480
00:16:38,130 --> 00:16:40,590
TAMON: You don't need to do anything like that.

481
00:16:40,590 --> 00:16:42,570
TAMON: We'd still make sure the show 
was plenty entertaining!

482
00:16:51,540 --> 00:16:53,500
OURI: We'll do our very best!

483
00:16:55,210 --> 00:16:57,360
NATSUKI: I am really scared, though.

484
00:16:59,100 --> 00:17:02,220
KEITO: F/ACE has the absolute best members.

485
00:17:02,220 --> 00:17:03,590
KEITO: You can count on us.

486
00:17:06,780 --> 00:17:08,680
ARIMOTO: Okay, let's do this.

487
00:17:08,680 --> 00:17:12,310
STAFF A: Sorry to keep everyone waiting! 
We'll now start the test of courage shoot!

488
00:17:12,310 --> 00:17:14,240
F/ACE: Thank you very much!

489
00:17:18,420 --> 00:17:21,290
UTAGE: They're finally starting 
their final shoot.

490
00:17:21,290 --> 00:17:23,200
UTAGE: Everything went by so fast.

491
00:17:23,470 --> 00:17:24,770
UTAGE: There we go.

492
00:17:26,560 --> 00:17:28,910
KEITO: They're making you do 
stuff like this, too?

493
00:17:28,910 --> 00:17:30,560
UTAGE: Tachibana-san.

494
00:17:30,560 --> 00:17:34,270
KEITO: Tamon doesn't like carrots, 
so remove those.

495
00:17:34,270 --> 00:17:35,720
KEITO: We don't want his real self peeking out.

496
00:17:36,150 --> 00:17:39,150
KEITO: Make sure the knives cut well, too.

497
00:17:39,150 --> 00:17:41,660
KEITO: He's insanely clumsy, 
so he'll get hurt otherwise.

498
00:17:41,660 --> 00:17:43,380
UTAGE: Understood.

499
00:17:43,380 --> 00:17:45,890
KEITO: Ugh, he's such a handful.

500
00:17:47,040 --> 00:17:51,350
UTAGE: You must actually really 
love Tamon-kun, Tachibana-san.

501
00:17:51,350 --> 00:17:52,440
KEITO: What?

502
00:17:52,440 --> 00:17:55,230
UTAGE: When you compliment Tamon-kun 
while you're all together as F/ACE, 

503
00:17:55,230 --> 00:17:57,070
UTAGE: that's genuine, isn't it?

504
00:17:57,640 --> 00:17:59,130
KEITO: Why do you think that?

505
00:17:59,490 --> 00:18:04,030
UTAGE: Because I don't think it's possible to 
move people's hearts with insincere words.

506
00:18:05,370 --> 00:18:08,110
UTAGE: You have a lot of fans, Keito-kun.

507
00:18:08,110 --> 00:18:11,330
UTAGE: Of course, you also have 
the most fans that are so passionate

508
00:18:11,330 --> 00:18:13,100
UTAGE: that they're a bit insane.

509
00:18:14,620 --> 00:18:16,850
UTAGE: Tamon-kun and Ouri-kun aren't lying

510
00:18:16,850 --> 00:18:20,410
UTAGE: when it comes to what's 
the most important.

511
00:18:20,410 --> 00:18:22,980
UTAGE: So I figured that you 
were probably the same way.

512
00:18:24,560 --> 00:18:25,750
KEITO: I...

513
00:18:26,050 --> 00:18:30,090
UTAGE: When you're a fan, both time 
and money melt away instantly.

514
00:18:30,110 --> 00:18:32,990
UTAGE: There's no time to spend 
anything on anyone shallow.

515
00:18:33,460 --> 00:18:35,740
KEITO: I'm just doing this for the money.

516
00:18:27,840 --> 00:18:30,600
TAMON: You sure are tall, Rintaro!

517
00:18:30,600 --> 00:18:33,460
NATSUKI: I'm super jealous. 
Gimme some of your height.

518
00:18:34,680 --> 00:18:36,650
STAFF A: Everyone, please get into your outfits!

519
00:18:36,650 --> 00:18:39,820
TAMON: We'll be right there! Let's do 
our best on this last shoot, guys!

520
00:18:39,820 --> 00:18:40,900
NATSUKI: Yeah!

521
00:18:41,540 --> 00:18:43,560
KEITO: Watching him pisses me off.

522
00:18:44,180 --> 00:18:47,200
KEITO: He's more awesome than anyone 
when he's got his shit together.

523
00:18:48,910 --> 00:18:53,440
UTAGE: Well, maybe you could try being 
a little nicer to him?

524
00:18:53,440 --> 00:18:55,640
KEITO: I don't need any advice from you.

525
00:18:57,360 --> 00:19:00,840
KEITO: I'm the leader of F/ACE, after all.

526
00:19:01,460 --> 00:19:02,430
UTAGE: You are.

527
00:19:02,800 --> 00:19:04,120
KEITO: I'm gonna go finish getting changed.

528
00:19:04,120 --> 00:19:05,000
UTAGE: Right!

529
00:19:12,890 --> 00:19:14,520
TAMON/OURI/NATSUKI: Ooh!

530
00:19:14,520 --> 00:19:16,520
TAMON: You're so good at cooking, Keito.

531
00:19:16,520 --> 00:19:20,360
KEITO: I used to help out in the kitchen 
when I worked at a café.

532
00:19:20,360 --> 00:19:23,070
KEITO: Not to mention, 
I have five little brothers, 

533
00:19:23,070 --> 00:19:26,530
KEITO: so I'd be in a kitchen a lot 
since my parents were always working.

534
00:19:27,820 --> 00:19:29,830
NATSUKI: Wait! You have five brothers?!

535
00:19:29,830 --> 00:19:31,910
OURI: I've never heard that before!

536
00:19:31,910 --> 00:19:33,960
KEITO: What? I never told you guys?

537
00:19:33,960 --> 00:19:35,150
TAMON: No?!

538
00:19:35,150 --> 00:19:36,610
KEITO: Oh, I see.

539
00:19:44,580 --> 00:19:46,900
UTAGE: And that's a wrap!

540
00:19:47,990 --> 00:19:49,950
UTAGE: I didn't know what to expect 
when I was told

541
00:19:49,950 --> 00:19:52,090
UTAGE: I'd be going to this training camp, but...

542
00:19:56,860 --> 00:19:59,430
UTAGE: I think things worked out
 surprisingly fine

543
00:19:59,430 --> 00:20:03,040
UTAGE: because Tamon-kun was pretty reliable.

544
00:20:03,860 --> 00:20:05,430
UTAGE: Gloomyhara-san!

545
00:20:05,430 --> 00:20:08,240
TAMON: Kinoshita-san! Are you on a break?

546
00:20:08,240 --> 00:20:10,410
UTAGE: Yes. What are you doing?

547
00:20:10,410 --> 00:20:12,240
TAMON: Well...

548
00:20:12,240 --> 00:20:15,060
TAMON: I know we're here for work, 
 but we came all the way to the ocean, 

549
00:20:15,060 --> 00:20:19,000
TAMON: and I was worried that you might not 
have gotten to do anything summery...

550
00:20:19,000 --> 00:20:20,950
TAMON: so I was taking pictures of the ocean.

551
00:20:20,950 --> 00:20:22,250
UTAGE: What?

552
00:20:22,250 --> 00:20:25,380
TAMON: I was going to show you later...

553
00:20:25,380 --> 00:20:26,410
TAMON: but look.

554
00:20:28,700 --> 00:20:32,180
UTAGE: A hermit crab...?

555
00:20:32,180 --> 00:20:34,890
TAMON: I'm so sorry I suck at taking pictures.

556
00:20:36,550 --> 00:20:38,400
TAMON: I do suck, don't I?!

557
00:20:38,400 --> 00:20:40,110
UTAGE: You don't.

558
00:20:40,110 --> 00:20:42,730
UTAGE: I just thought this was 
very much like you, Gloomyhara-san.

559
00:20:43,000 --> 00:20:45,790
TAMON: Th-Thank you very much.

560
00:20:54,310 --> 00:20:59,040
TAMON: Today, I found out why Keito-kun became 
an idol for the first time.

561
00:20:59,040 --> 00:21:00,600
UTAGE: Tachibana-san?

562
00:21:00,600 --> 00:21:04,590
TAMON: He always mentioned that it was 
for money, but it's actually...

563
00:21:04,900 --> 00:21:07,590
KEITO: My brothers have middle school, 
high school, 

564
00:21:07,590 --> 00:21:09,410
KEITO: and uni entrance exams coming up.

565
00:21:09,720 --> 00:21:12,870
KEITO: And um... I wanted to 
help out my parents a bit.

566
00:21:13,290 --> 00:21:15,720
TAMON: It was so his family could smile.

567
00:21:16,400 --> 00:21:20,890
TAMON: I want to do my best with Keito-kun 
as the center of F/ACE.

568
00:21:25,040 --> 00:21:28,820
UTAGE: I'll do everything I can to support 
the brand new F/ACE, too!

569
00:21:35,600 --> 00:21:36,740
TAMON: Kinoshita-san!

570
00:21:38,480 --> 00:21:40,090
UTAGE: So cold!

571
00:21:49,050 --> 00:21:52,010
TAMON: Are you okay? You should probably 
change before you catch a cold.

572
00:21:52,010 --> 00:21:54,900
UTAGE: I wouldn't catch a cold from this!

573
00:21:55,470 --> 00:21:58,430
UTAGE: I slept like a rock 
last night, so I'm fine!

574
00:21:58,430 --> 00:21:59,490
TAMON: Oh...

575
00:22:01,810 --> 00:22:03,270
TAMON: You're right.

576
00:22:04,350 --> 00:22:06,860
TAMON: Your complexion looks much better today.

577
00:22:26,920 --> 00:22:30,170
LYRICS: Uh huh...

578
00:22:30,170 --> 00:22:32,220
LYRICS: Na na na...

579
00:22:32,220 --> 00:22:35,260
LYRICS: Uh huh...

580
00:22:37,390 --> 00:22:46,810
LYRICS: I wonder what the world 
would look like without you

581
00:22:47,650 --> 00:22:52,530
LYRICS: When I look back, 
you've always been by my side

582
00:22:52,530 --> 00:22:57,450
LYRICS: Teaching me what "warmth" 
and "happiness" feel like

583
00:22:57,450 --> 00:23:00,240
LYRICS: A speedboat sails across the endless skies

584
00:23:00,240 --> 00:23:02,790
LYRICS: An unwavering course, 
a straight shot down the middle

585
00:23:02,790 --> 00:23:05,420
LYRICS: An unbreakable red balloon 
found nowhere else

586
00:23:05,420 --> 00:23:08,670
LYRICS: Is this "fate"? Or just a "coincidence"?

587
00:23:08,960 --> 00:23:13,760
LYRICS: Like a wilted flower coming back to life

588
00:23:13,760 --> 00:23:16,300
LYRICS: A light that shines

589
00:23:16,300 --> 00:23:19,300
LYRICS: Through the impossibly dark night

590
00:23:19,300 --> 00:23:20,600
LYRICS: (Light of your soul)

591
00:23:20,600 --> 00:23:21,970
LYRICS: I wanted to grasp it

592
00:23:21,970 --> 00:23:23,270
LYRICS: (I love you so)

593
00:23:23,270 --> 00:23:24,310
LYRICS: So I strived for it

594
00:23:24,310 --> 00:23:27,020
LYRICS: Wanna keep going, wanna keep growing

595
00:23:27,020 --> 00:23:30,820
LYRICS: Bringing our flowers and dreams 
into full bloom

596
